          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "399911",
          "text": "<p>Two integers have the same parity if they are both even or they are both odd. Otherwise, they have opposite parity. Which of the following statements is/are true?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>If two integers have the same parity, their sum is odd.</li><li>If two integers have opposite parity, then their sum is odd.</li><li>If $n$ is an odd integer, then $8 \\mid n^2-1$.</li><li>Suppose $a, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}$. If $a b$ is odd, then $a^2+b^2$ is even.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "b;c;d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq1,goclasses,quantitative-aptitude,algebra,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "399928",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following statements:</p><ul><li>$\\text{S1}:$ Suppose $a, b, c \\in \\mathbb{Z}$. If $a^2 \\mid b$ and $b^3 \\mid c,$ then $a^6 \\mid c$.</li><li>$\\text{S2}:$ Suppose $a \\in \\mathbb{Z}$. If $a^3$ is not divisible by $8,$ then $a$ is odd.</li></ul><p>Which of the above statements is true?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>Only $\\text{S1}$.</li><li>Only $\\text{S2}$.</li><li>Both $\\text{S1}&nbsp;\\;\\&amp; \\;\\text{S2}$.</li><li>None</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq1,goclasses,quantitative-aptitude,algebra,one-mark",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "399922",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following statements:</p><ul><li>$\\text{S1}:$ If an integer ' $a$ ' is even then $\\left(a^ 2\\right)+2 a+9$ is odd.</li><li>$\\text{S2}:$ For an integer ' $a$ ', if $\\left(a^ 2\\right)+2 a+9$ is odd then ' $a$ ' is even.</li></ul><p>Which of the above statements is true?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>Only $\\text{S1}$</li><li>Only $\\text{S2}$</li><li>Both $\\text{S1}\\;&nbsp;\\&amp;\\; \\text{S2}$</li><li>None</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq1,goclasses,quantitative-aptitude,algebra,one-mark",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "399917",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following right-angled triangle, in which the angle between the side $\\text{AC}$ and $\\text{CB}$ is a right angle. Let $a,b,c$ be the length of the sides $\\text{BC, AC, AB}$ respectively. Assume $a,b,c$ are integers.</p><p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"height:191px; width:215px\"></p><p>Which of the following is/are correct statements?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>$(abc)$ is even.</li><li>$(bc)$ is even.</li><li>$(ab)$ or $(ac)$ is even.</li><li>Both $a,b$ are even.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "A;C",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq1,goclasses,quantitative-aptitude,geometry,triangles,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "399920",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following statements:</p><ul><li>$\\text{S1}:$ Given any $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$, there exists an element $y \\in \\mathbb{R}$ for which $x y=1$.</li><li>$\\text{S2}:$ There exists two irrational numbers $x$ and $y$ such that $x+y$ is rational.</li></ul><p>Which of the above statements is true?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>Only $\\text{S1}$</li><li>Only $\\text{S2}$</li><li>Both $\\text{S1}\\; \\&amp;\\; \\text{S2}$</li><li>None</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq1,goclasses,quantitative-aptitude,algebra,one-mark",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
