        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "399915",
          "text": "<p>Let $n$ be a positive integer.</p><p>Which of the following statements is/are true?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>If $m, a$ are positive integers and $m \\mid a^ n$, then $m^ n \\mid a^ n$.</li><li>If $p$ is a prime and $a$ is a positive integer and $p \\mid a^n$, then $p^n \\mid a^n$.</li><li>If $t$ is odd, then $t^ n$ is also odd, for all $n$.</li><li>If $t$ is even, then $t^ n$ is also even, for all $n$.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "b;c;d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq1,goclasses,quantitative-aptitude,algebra,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "399919",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is/are True?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>If $x$ and $y$ are two integers whose product is odd, then both must be odd.</li><li>If $a$ and $b$ are real numbers such that the product ab is an irrational number, then either $a$ or&nbsp;$b$ must be an irrational number.</li><li>For any integer $m,$ if $m^{2}$ is even, then $m$ is even.</li><li>The sum of a rational number and an irrational number is irrational.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;c;d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq1,goclasses,quantitative-aptitude,algebra,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Quantitative Aptitude"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "399924",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following statements:</p><ul><li>$\\text{S1}:$ Suppose $a, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}$. If $\\left(a^ 2\\right)\\left(b^ 2-2 b\\right)$ is odd, then both $a$ and $b$ are odd.</li><li>$\\text{S2}:$ Suppose $a, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}$. If $25 \\nmid a b$, then $5 \\nmid a$ or $5 \\nmid b$.</li></ul><p>Which of the above statements is true?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>Only $\\text{S1}$</li><li>Only $\\text{S2}$</li><li>Both $\\text{S1}\\;&nbsp;\\&amp;\\; \\text{S2}$</li><li>None</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq1,goclasses,quantitative-aptitude,algebra,one-mark",
