          "text": "<p>Consider the following statements:</p><ul><li>$\\text{S1}:$ If $a, b \\in Z$ and $a+b$ is even, then $a^ 2+b^ 2$ is even.</li><li>$\\text{S2}:$ If $a, b \\in Z$ and $a+b$ is odd, then $a^ 2+b^ 2$ is odd.</li></ul><p>Which of the above statements is true?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>Only $\\text{S1}$</li><li>Only $\\text{S2}$</li><li>Both $\\text{S1}\\;&nbsp;\\&amp;\\; \\text{S2}$</li><li>None</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
